                "username": "faisal-awada"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/registry/message_registry.json",
                    "line": 2295,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "Since the update succeeded, it seems like it maybe shouldn't have \"Error\" in the name.\n\nI see an entry in this file called \"xyz.openbmc_project.State.Info.ChassisPowerOnStarted\"\n\nSo maybe replace \".Error.\" with \".Info.\" ?\n\nWill defer to Matt on this.  Customers can probably see these Name values, so I just don't want them asking support why they have these \"errors\"."
                },
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/registry/message_registry.json",
                    "line": 2295,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "They had .Error. in the name, because these were based on the Message property values you'd get when you'd use the built in elog<>, commit<>, report<>, etc for errors defined with the D-Bus YAML.  \n\nThese don't show up anywhere though, so it doesn't really matter. If you were creating these in a common upstream repository, you'd probably need to move to use the new event YAML that was recently introduced instead of manually calling Logging.Create.  And I suppose there's still a chance someone could come in here and change all of these.\n\nAlso, the new event yaml doesn't have .Error. segment at all so removing it here is fine."
                },
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/registry/message_registry.json",
                    "line": 2295,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Faisal Awada",
                        "email": "faisal@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "faisal-awada"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/registry/message_registry.json",
                    "line": 2330,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "The name \"BmcFirmwareUpdateFailed\" sounds like the error occurred while trying to update the BMC firmware.\n\nSince the error already has PowerSupply earlier in the name, should we just remove \"Bmc\"?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/registry/message_registry.json",
                    "line": 2330,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Faisal Awada",
                        "email": "faisal@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "faisal-awada"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
